<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Komotini</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gümülcine</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Komotini is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-thrace">Western Thrace</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, capital of the region of Eastern Macedonia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>. Under Ottoman rule, as Gümülcine, it had a mainly Muslim population, and in 1913 it was the seat of the short-lived Provisional Government of Western Thrace. It passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> and then to Greece in 1920, and it remains the centre of Greece's Muslim minority.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/komotini.jpg" alt="Komotini" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pitichinaccio · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2011_Dimos_Komotinis.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
